cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite our paper as below."
title: "BOLT: Online Lightweight Adaptation for Preparation-Free Heterogeneous Cooperative Perception"
abstract: >-
  Most existing heterogeneous cooperative perception methods depend on prior preparation
  such as offline joint training or tailored collaborator-model adaptation, which is
  generally impractical when agents are independently trained by different developers.
  We study preparation-free heterogeneous cooperative perception, where agents use
  independently trained single-agent detectors with no pre-deployment coordination,
  and show that direct cross-agent fusion in this setting greatly underperforms ego-only
  perception. We present BOLT, a lightweight plug-and-play module that adapts incoming
  neighbor features online via ego-as-teacher distillation, using only ego predictions
  without ground-truth labels. With only 0.9M trainable parameters, BOLT improves AP@50
  by up to 32.3 points over unadapted fusion and consistently outperforms ego-only
  results on DAIR-V2X and OPV2V across different encoder pairs and fusion strategies.
